>> title: Stefan's One-Pot Golden Pork & Cheese Pillows
>> description: Juicy, deeply browned pork coated in a smoky tomato glaze, paired with melted Gouda and wrapped in crispy, golden tortilla pockets. Easy to make, packed with flavour, and perfect for meal prep. Minimal cleanup, maximum satisfaction.
>> servings: 7
>> tags: pork, lunch, dinner, meal prep
>> time: 70 minutes

Finely dice the @onion{100%g}. Cut the @boneless pork shoulder{800%g} into small, bite-sized pieces. Choose a cut with a good amount of fat, as this will make the filling richer and more flavourful.

Heat the @sunflower oil{2%tbsp} in a medium-to-large pot over high heat. Add the diced onion and cook for ~{4-6%minutes}, stirring occasionally, until deeply golden brown and almost caramelised.

Add the pork and season with @salt{1.5%tsp}, @pepper{2%tsp}, @sweet paprika{2%tsp}, @{garlic powder%1tsp}, @Vegeta{1.5%tsp}, and @oregano{1%tsp}. The pork will initially release some liquid. Continue cooking until all the liquid has evaporated, then keep cooking until the meat is deeply browned and slightly caramelised. This should take approximately ~{30%minutes} in total.

Stir in the @tomato sauce{200%g} and @smokey BBQ sauce{2%tbsp}. Continue cooking, stirring occasionally, until the excess liquid has evaporated and the sauce has reduced to a thick glaze that lightly coats the meat. There should be no sauce pooling at the bottom of the pot. This takes approximately ~{15%minutes}.

While the filling finishes cooking, arrange the @tortilla wraps{7%pieces} on a clean, flat surface. Place 2 slices of @Gouda cheese{14%slices} in the centre of each tortilla, slightly overlapping. Alternatively, stack the tortillas on a large plate and assemble them one at a time to save space.

Once the filling is ready, add about 2 tablespoons of the filling on top of the cheese in each tortilla. Spread it into a flat layer roughly the size of the two cheese slices.

Fold two opposite sides of each tortilla towards the centre, then fold the remaining two sides over them to form a sealed pocket. Make sure all the edges are tucked in securely, with no filling or cheese exposed.

Use the hot oil remaining in the pot to crisp up the pillows. Place each one seam-side down first and fry for ~{30%seconds}, allowing the folds to seal together. Carefully flip and fry the other side for another ~{30%seconds}, or until both sides are lightly golden and crispy.

Serve warm with fresh tomato on the side and a creamy dip. Sour cream, aioli, or a simple mixture of sour cream, mayonnaise, and garlic all work beautifully.

For meal prep, let the pillows cool completely, wrap them individually in plastic wrap, and freeze. When ready to eat, remove the wrapping and microwave straight from frozen for ~{2-3%minutes}, or until heated through.
